# --- Python standard ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.Python
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store

# --- FinScreen data cache ---
# data/raw/ holds cached raw EDGAR JSON responses (submissions dumps, filing
# indices, the bulk ticker map). It is fully regenerable by re-running the
# ingestion script against data/universe.csv (idempotent, same rate-limited
# client) and can grow to tens/hundreds of MB across the universe, so it is
# excluded from version control rather than committed.
#
# data/universe.csv IS versioned deliberately -- it's the locked, hand-chosen
# company list and is not regenerable from anything else.
#
# data/filings_metadata.db (SQLite) is a small, deterministic derived
# artifact (a few thousand rows of filing metadata) -- it is NOT excluded
# here so the ingested metadata snapshot is reproducible/inspectable without
# re-hitting EDGAR, but if it grows large in later weeks this choice should
# be revisited.
data/raw/

# --- Bulk / regenerable artifacts (added for public GitHub push) ---
# Batch API request payloads: ~308 MB across variants, three of them 77 MB
# each (over GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold). Fully regenerable by
# re-running build_batch_requests.py against data/labeling_corpus.parquet.
data/*.jsonl

# Derived text/price corpora. Regenerable from data/raw/ via extract.py +
# chunk.py, and from the price client, respectively.
data/filings.parquet
data/labeling_corpus.parquet
data/prices.parquet
data/paragraph_occurrence_map.parquet

# Bootstrap label sets. NOTE: unlike everything else here, these are NOT
# free to regenerate -- they cost real Batch API spend. They are excluded to
# keep the repo lean, which means git is NOT a backup for them. Keep an
# independent copy. To version them instead, delete the four lines below.
data/labels.parquet
data/labels_pre_relabel.parquet
data/labels_relabel.parquet
data/labels_corrective.parquet
# The rubric-v1.2 re-label (2026-08-26, G1 repair campaign). Same warning, and
# stronger: the account's prepaid credits were drained producing it and the
# spend freeze is re-sealed, so it is NOT re-buyable. Keep an independent copy.
data/labels_v12.parquet

# --- E2 ingestion outputs (F2, added 2026-08-24) ---
# All regenerable at $0 by re-running the idempotent S6 segments against the
# cache; sized past GitHub's warning threshold (fundamentals_e2 ~25-60 MB,
# prices_e2 ~40-80 MB, the E2 metadata DB covers ~45k filings). E1's
# filings_metadata.db stays versioned per the note above; the E2 DB is the
# "grows large" case that note anticipated.
data/filings_metadata_e2.db
data/fundamentals_e2.parquet
data/prices_e2.parquet
data/filings_e2.parquet

# Fine-tune datasets: 41 MB, deterministically derived from labels.parquet
# via finetune/prepare_dataset.py and finetune/split.py (seeded splits).
finetune/prepared/
finetune/splits/
# Same, for the rubric-v1.2 retrain (2026-08-26). splits_v12 is derived from
# labels_v12.parquet by JOIN onto the frozen finetune/splits/manifest.parquet
# (finetune/build_splits_v12.py); prepared_v12 from it by prepare_dataset.py.
# Their build_report.json / conversion_report.json ARE small enough to keep,
# and the run directory's dataset_manifest.json carries every sha.
finetune/splits_v12/*.parquet
finetune/prepared_v12/

# --- MLX local fine-tune (finetune/MLX_FEASIBILITY.md) ---
# Dedicated venv for the mlx/mlx-lm stack -- kept separate from the repo's
# main requirements.txt env by design. Not committed (like any venv).
finetune/.mlx_venv/
# mlx-format train.jsonl/valid.jsonl converted from finetune/prepared/ --
# deterministically regenerable, same reasoning as finetune/prepared/ above.
finetune/mlx_data/
finetune/mlx_data_v12/*.jsonl
# LoRA adapter checkpoints + optimizer state written during training.
finetune/checkpoints/
# Downloaded MLX-format base model weights (~4 GiB), if ever cached inside
# the repo instead of the default huggingface_hub cache (~/.cache/huggingface).
finetune/mlx_models/

# --- E2 extraction + labeling bulk artifacts (F3/F4; added 2026-09-07 for the
# GitHub push). Rule: nothing over GitHub's 50 MB warning line, nothing that is a
# byte-copy of a consolidated artifact. Every excluded file's sha256 is pinned in
# a committed manifest, so provenance survives even though the bytes do not.
#
# F3 extraction shards (~1.2 GB across the two shard dirs) and the consolidated
# corpus data/filings_e2_v2.parquet (599 MB; sha 15853e9f…, pinned in F4 prep)
# are the same data twice; regenerable at $0 from data/raw/ via extract.py.
# Everything else under data/f3/ (status ledgers, QA reports, audits, CSVs,
# manifests, fixtures) is kept.
data/f3/shards/
data/f3/v2/shards/
data/filings_e2_v2.parquet
# F4: the chunk table (382 MB; regenerable from filings_e2_v2 by
# finetune/label_e2.py) and the campaign's consolidated student labels (417 MB;
# NOT cheap to regenerate — 24 segments, ~9 GPU overnights; git is not a backup
# for it, keep an independent copy). shas: data/f4/campaign_manifest.json and
# data/f4/g2/build_draw_g2.py INPUT_SHA256. The per-segment outputs
# (rows.jsonl / labels.jsonl / labels_seg-NNN.parquet, ~60 MB per segment × 24)
# are those same labels before consolidation; each segment's manifest.json and
# seg.log are kept, as is everything under data/f4/g2/ and data/f4/status/.
data/f4/chunks_v1.parquet
data/f4/labels_e2_v1.parquet
data/f4/segments/*/rows.jsonl
data/f4/segments/*/labels.jsonl
data/f4/segments/*/labels_seg-*.parquet
data/f4/smoke/rows.jsonl
data/f4/smoke/labels*.jsonl
data/f4/smoke/*.parquet
# 9.6 MB pre-completion snapshot of labels_v12.parquet (itself excluded above).
data/labels_v12.parquet.pre_completion
# H3 / H3v2 student re-labels of the E1 corpus (two 9.4 MB parquets + two 3.3 MB
# jsonl; regenerable in ~5 GPU hours by finetune/relabel_e1.py). Their derived
# feature tables, sidecars, manifests and status reports are kept.
data/hardening/e1_relabel_student.parquet
data/hardening/e1_relabel_student.jsonl
data/hardening/h3v2/e1_relabel_student_v12.parquet
data/hardening/h3v2/e1_relabel_student_v12.jsonl

# --- F5 outputs (added 2026-09-10) ---
# Feature / target tables built by features_e2.py, numeric_features_e2.py and
# target_e2.py are regenerable from the F4 labels + F2 ingestion outputs at $0;
# their sha256s are recorded in data/f5/*_manifest.json, which IS versioned,
# as are the status reports, census, and the G3 pre-registration.
data/f5/*.parquet
data/f5/**/*.parquet
